==English==

===Etymology===
From the expression ''the [[early bird catches the worm]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-early bird.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A [[person]] who [[wake]]s [[early]] or [[arrive]]s early, typically before most others.
#* '''1974''', [[w:Shel Silverstein|Shel Silverstein]], “'''Early Bird'''”, ''[[w:Where the Sidewalk Ends (book)|Where the Sidewalk Ends]]'', HarperCollins:
#*: If you’re a bird, be an '''early bird'''— But if you’re a worm, sleep late.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|one who wakes early}} {{l|en|early riser}}, {{l|en|morning person}}
Anybody other then B Miller

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|nighthawk}}, {{l|en|night owl}}, {{l|en|night person}}, {{l|en|late riser}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|the early bird catches the worm}}

